---@field default_variation string Variation the API serves when the flag is off, or when it's on but no rule matches the context. Must be a key in `variations`.
---@field enabled boolean When false, the flag bypasses all rules and always serves `default_variation`.
---@field key string Unique identifier for the flag within an app. Used in all evaluation and SDK calls.
---@field rules cloudflare.flagship.AppsFlagsCreateRequestRulesList Targeting rules evaluated in ascending `priority`; the first matching rule wins. An empty array means the flag always serves `default_variation`.
---@field variations cloudflare.flagship.UntypedVariationsMap Map of variation name to value. All values share the same type (boolean, string, number, or JSON object/array), and each serialized value stays within 10KB.
---@field description? string Optional operator-facing description. It does not affect flag evaluation.
---@field metadata? cloudflare.flagship.AppsFlagsCreateRequestMetadataMap Key-value metadata associated with the flag. `null` or an empty object clears existing metadata; omission semantics depend on the endpoint (PUT clears it, PATCH preserves it).
---@field type? cloudflare.flagship.AppsFlagsCreateRequestType|string Deprecated compatibility field. Omit it; the API ignores this value and infers the type from the flag's variations.

